<Project Sdk="Microsoft.NET.Sdk">

  <!-- CONCEPTS-REF 25, PROVED as far as a console can prove it - and explicit
       about where that stops.

       25 makes a text box carry a colour and asks that colour to survive to
       four places: the live XAML editor, the 16.7 veil, the Win2D raster and
       the two vector exporters. THREE of those four need a window and cannot be
       measured here. What can be measured is the fourth, and it is the one the
       brief named as the row that matters most:

         "recolour a text box, export to PDF and SVG, and confirm the colour
          survives both. Failure there looks like perfect on screen and black in
          the file."

       So this tool measures two things, against the real code:

         1. THE PAGE'S INK RULE (PageTheme.TextInk). The rule that decides what
            colour a box with NO colour of its own is drawn in was four copies
            of one ternary; it is now one function, and one function can be
            swept. The sweep reproduces the numbers 25.4 quotes rather than
            trusting them, and it runs the REJECTED alternative alongside so the
            rejection is a measurement and not an opinion.

         2. THE COLOUR REACHING THE FILE. Two boxes with two different colours
            on one page, through the real PdfExporter and the real
            HtmlSvgExporter, read back out of the inflated PDF content stream
            and out of the SVG parsed as XML. The pre-25 behaviour - one
            page-wide inkHex for every box - is built alongside and is REQUIRED
            TO FAIL the same check, so the harness is shown to be able to go red
            rather than merely observed to be green.

       Nothing below is a re-typed copy. PageTheme, ColorUtil and both emitters
       are <Compile Include>d straight out of src/Quill. Written to the pattern
       tools/ExportRotRoundTrip set, and isolated the same way it is: this tool
       never touches LibraryStore, so it has no library to be isolated from and
       cannot reach the user's.

       net8.0-windows10.0.19041.0 to match its siblings. Nothing here needs a
       window - PageTheme, ColorUtil and the two emitters are plain BCL over
       Windows.UI.Color, which is the reason this layer can be measured at
       all. -->

  <PropertyGroup>
    <OutputType>Exe</OutputType>
    <TargetFramework>net8.0-windows10.0.19041.0</TargetFramework>
    <Platforms>x64</Platforms>
    <RuntimeIdentifier>win-x64</RuntimeIdentifier>
    <SelfContained>false</SelfContained>
    <Nullable>enable</Nullable>
    <ImplicitUsings>enable</ImplicitUsings>
    <RootNamespace>Quill.Tools</RootNamespace>
    <AssemblyName>TextColourRoundTrip</AssemblyName>
    <EnableDefaultCompileItems>false</EnableDefaultCompileItems>
  </PropertyGroup>

  <ItemGroup>
    <Compile Include="Program.cs" />
    <!-- The rule under test, and the ColorUtil.IsDark it replaces - the real
         one, so "no existing note changes colour" is a comparison and not a
         claim. -->
    <Compile Include="..\..\src\Quill\Services\PageTheme.cs" Link="PageTheme.cs" />
    <Compile Include="..\..\src\Quill\Helpers\Util.cs" Link="Util.cs" />
    <!-- The two emitters, and the font resolver PdfExporter calls. -->
    <Compile Include="..\..\src\Quill\Services\PdfExporter.cs" Link="PdfExporter.cs" />
    <Compile Include="..\..\src\Quill\Services\HtmlSvgExporter.cs" Link="HtmlSvgExporter.cs" />
    <Compile Include="..\..\src\Quill\Services\FontSubsetter.cs" Link="FontSubsetter.cs" />
  </ItemGroup>

</Project>
